From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadim Bauer <vb@container-registry.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:00:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(registry/handlers): add Harbor GC delete endpoints

Harbor's garbage collection removes blob data and manifest revisions that
no repository references anymore. The v2 API cannot do that: DELETE
/v2/<name>/blobs/<digest> only unlinks a blob from one repository. Harbor
ran a separate registryctl sidecar for it, built against distribution
v2.8.2 and its own copy of the storage driver configuration.

Serve the same endpoints from the registry itself:

  DELETE /api/registry/blob/<digest>
  DELETE /api/registry/<name>/manifests/<digest>
  GET    /api/health

The delete routes require "Authorization: Harbor-Secret <JOBSERVICE_SECRET>".
They are only registered when JOBSERVICE_SECRET is set, so a registry
without it behaves like upstream.

Deleting a blob also clears its blob descriptor cache entry. With the
redis cache, repository scoped lookups read that global entry, so a
re-push of the deleted content uploads the blob again instead of being
answered from a stale cache entry.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Bauer <vb@container-registry.com>
Upstream: none, Harbor specific
Signed-off-by: Vadim Bauer <vb@container-registry.com>
---
